event.text:
User feedback: the chooser links currently scroll down to the expanded panel (`#sheet-path` / `#group-path`), but they want the links to scroll to the "How do you want to collect orders?" section (the `#start` entry-choice section with both path cards), with the corresponding option card selected/highlighted.

So change `goToPath` targets from panel IDs to the `start` section. `selectPath(which)` already toggles the `.on` class on the chosen card and unhides the panel below. So: call `selectPath(which)`, then scroll to `#start` (the entry-choice section) instead of the panel.

Should I also move focus? Focus heading `#start-h`. The "How do you want to collect orders?" heading is `h2#start-h` inside `section#start.entry-choice`.

Update app.js:

```js
if ($('onboarding-go-sheet')) {
  $('onboarding-go-sheet').addEventListener('click', () => goToPath('sheet'));
}
if ($('onboarding-go-group')) {
  $('onboarding-go-group').addEventListener('click', () => goToPath('group'));
}
```

And goToPath:

```js
/* The chooser answers link back to the collection choice with that option
   selected, so the organizer sees which path opened below. */
function goToPath(which) {
  selectPath(which);
  const choice = $('start');
  if (!choice) return;
  if (choice.scrollIntoView) {
    try { choice.scrollIntoView({ behavior: 'smooth', block: 'start' }); }
    catch (error) { choice.scrollIntoView(); }
  }
  const heading = $('start-h');
  if (heading && heading.focus) {
    try { heading.setAttribute('tabindex', '-1'); heading.focus({ preventScroll: true }); }
    catch (error) { /* visual only */ }
  }
}
```

Wait — will the selected card be visibly "selected"? `selectPath` toggles `on` class on the path cards. Check CSS: `.path-card.on { border-color: var(--accent); box-shadow: ... }`. Yes, visible highlight. Good — the selected option shows highlighted at the "How do you want to collect orders?" section, and the corresponding panel opens below the fold.

Update the comment and the doc line ("each answer linking straight to its section" → "each answer selects its option in the collection choice"). Update docs/task23-onboarding.md accordingly.

Also verify live. Make edits.

